ign initiated in response to the September 11 attacks, was a pivotal event in global history. It began on September 11, 2001, with the coordinated terrorist attacks on the World Trade Center in New York City and the Pentagon in Washington, D.C., resulting in nearly 3,000 deaths. The subsequent US-led military operations in Afghanistan and Iraq, which lasted until August 30, 2021, had far-reaching consequences, including the displacement of millions of people, the deaths of thousands of soldiers and civilians, and a significant escalation of global terrorism. The War on Terror also marked a significant turning point in the history of the Middle East, as it led to the overthrow of governments in Afghanistan and Iraq, and contributed to the rise of extremist groups like ISIS.

